WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.660
So what memories or stories did your grandparents or parents tell you about the storm of 1893?

2
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:13.120
Well, in 1893 my grandma survived.

3
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.460
My grandma was eleven years old and there were nothing on this island.

4
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.540
Everything was across the bridge.

5
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.680
As a matter of fact, LSU was building a place.

6
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:31.940
They were going to have students going there and all, but that was wiped out.

7
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.420
There was no other industry but seafood then.

8
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:42.320
And she told me that at three o'clock the day before the storm she'd look under and the tide was real low.

9
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.960
People was picking up soft-shelled crabs on the flat.

10
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.860
And she said there was something about that sun that they'd never seen before, it was red.

11
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.760
Fire-ball red.

12
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:58.920
And three o'clock the next morning, over sixteen-hundred people was drowned.

13
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.940
You didn't have the weather report or this, no, no.

14
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.700
Back to . . . You say your grandmother was a survivor of the storm?

15
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.160
Yeah.

16
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.720
Did they tell you anything about water coming up on the island?

17
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.100
Oh, she said it was a mess.

18
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.900
She always said, "Whenever we got a storm, leave if you can.

19
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.980
Because once it's there, all you're doing is praying to God.

20
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:30.300
And it's so dark you can't see your hand and the noise of the wind wants to bust your eardrums up," she said.

21
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.020
After the storm they moved up the bayou for a while.

22
00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:39.180
But she lost her mom, her daddy, and one brother survived.

23
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.080
Her and her brother survived and the rest all drowned.

24
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:51.020
They find people sixteen days after, the ship picks them up in the riptide in the Gulf.

25
00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:51.640
It was bad.
